    <article class="doc">
        <h2 id="operating-model">Operating model</h2>

        <p>
            A port is a directory containing a <code>build.eme</code> recipe and
            optional metadata. The recipe declares identity, source archives,
            checksums, dependencies, and a POSIX <code>build()</code> function.
            Emerald builds into a package archive, installs it through the
            package database, and runs system triggers as needed.
        </p>

        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Task</th>
                    <th>Command</th>
                    <th>Effect</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>

            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Refresh metadata</td>

                    <td>
                        <code>emerald sync</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Update configured ports repositories.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Install</td>

                    <td>
                        <code>emerald install pkg</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Build or fetch, resolve dependencies, and install.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Upgrade one</td>

                    <td>
                        <code>emerald upgrade pkg</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Upgrade a selected installed port.</td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>Upgrade system</td>

                    <td>
                        <code>emerald sysup</code>
                    </td>

                    <td>Upgrade all eligible installed ports.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="help">
            <code>emerald help</code>
        </h2>

        <pre><code>Usage:
    emerald &lt;options&gt; [&lt;arg&gt;]

Options:
    search       &lt;pattern&gt;         find ports in repo
                                   -n, --name   search in port names only

    sync                   &lt;arg&gt;   update ports database (use portsync arg)
                                   -p, --prune  prune local git repository
                                   -r, --reset  reset git repositories

    build        &lt;ports&gt;   &lt;arg&gt;   build ports (use pkgbuild arg, except '-i', '-u', '-r', '-g', &amp; '-p')
                                   -f           force rebuild package
                                   -m           skip checksum checking
                                   -o           fetch sources only
                                   -q, --quiet  show only status messages and errors
                                   -w           keep working directory
                                   -y           skip ask user confirmation
                                   -C, --clean  remove downloaded sources and prebuilt packages
                                   --log        log build process (/var/log/name-version-release-date.log)
                                   --jobs=&lt;N&gt;   override parallel build jobs (default: JOBS in config, or nproc)

    install      &lt;ports&gt;   &lt;arg&gt;   install ports (use pkgbuild arg, except '-i' &amp; '-u')
                                   -c           ignore conflict when installing package
                                   -f           force rebuild package
                                   -m           skip checksum checking
                                   -n           skip dependencies
                                   -o           fetch sources only
                                   -q, --quiet  show only status messages and errors
                                   -r           reinstall
                                   -w           keep working directory
                                   -y, --yes    skip ask user confirmation
                                   --exclude=*  exclude dependencies, comma separated
                                   --no-backup  skip backup when reinstalling package
                                   --jobs=&lt;N&gt;   override parallel build jobs (default: JOBS in config, or nproc)

    upgrade      &lt;ports&gt;   &lt;arg&gt;   upgrade ports (use pkgbuild arg, except '-i' &amp; '-r')
                                   -c           ignore conflict when installing package
                                   -f           force rebuild package
                                   -m           skip checksum checking
                                   -n           skip dependencies
                                   -o           fetch sources only
                                   -q, --quiet  show only status messages and errors
                                   -w           keep working directory
                                   -y, --yes    skip ask user confirmation
                                   --exclude=*  exclude dependencies, comma separated
                                   --no-backup  skip backup when upgrading package
                                   --jobs=&lt;N&gt;   override parallel build jobs (default: JOBS in config, or nproc)

    sysup                  &lt;arg&gt;   full system upgrade (use pkgbuild arg, except '-i', '-r'  &amp; '-u')
                                   -c           ignore conflict when installing package
                                   -f           force rebuild package
                                   -m           skip checksum checking
                                   -n           skip dependencies
                                   -o           fetch sources only
                                   -q, --quiet  show only status messages and errors
                                   -w           keep working directory
                                   -y, --yes    skip ask user confirmation
                                   --exclude=*  exclude dependencies, comma separated
                                   --no-backup  skip backup when upgrading package
                                   --jobs=&lt;N&gt;   override parallel build jobs (default: JOBS in config, or nproc)

    remove       &lt;ports&gt;   &lt;arg&gt;   remove installed ports (use pkgdel arg)
                                   -y, --yes    skip ask user confirmation

    deplist      &lt;ports&gt;           print all dependencies for ports
                                   -q, --quick  skip installed ports
                                   --exclude=*  exclude dependencies, comma separated

    redeps       &lt;ports&gt;   &lt;arg&gt;   find redundant dependencies
                                   -w, --world  check redundant entries in world
                                   -f, --fix    fix (remove) redundant port deps / world entries

    cache                          (no args)    clean packages AND sources cache
                                   -p, --pkg    clean packages cache only
                                   -s, --src    clean sources cache only

    cat          &lt;port&gt;            print $BUILD_SCRIPT
    config                         print emerald config
    dependent    &lt;port&gt;            print reverse dependencies
    depends      &lt;port&gt;            print dependencies
    conflicts    &lt;port&gt;            print conflicting ports
    dup                            print duplicate ports
    files        &lt;port&gt;            print files installed
    foreign                        print foreign ports
    help                           print this help
    hook  &lt;stage&gt; &lt;action&gt; &lt;port&gt;  run port hook on demand (run 'emerald hook' for help)
    info         &lt;port&gt;            print information
    installed                      print all installed ports
    integrity                      check installed port integrity
    is-installed  &lt;port&gt;           check whether port is installed (status 0=installed, 1=not installed)
    locate       &lt;file&gt;            print location of file in ports repo
    alias        &lt;arg&gt;             manage aliased ports (run 'emerald alias help' for usage)
    mask         &lt;arg&gt;             manage masked ports (run 'emerald mask help' for usage)
    missing-deps                   print missing dependencies
    orphan                         print orphan installed ports
    outdated                       print outdated ports
    path         &lt;port&gt;            print path in repo
    provide      &lt;file&gt;            print ports provided file
    purge        [ports]           remove installed ports and its orphan dependencies
    trigger      [ports]           run system trigger
    world        [ports]           print/add/remove world list
    list                           print all available ports
    version                        print version information and exit

Global options:
    --append-repo=&lt;repo path&gt;      append custom local repo path (can use multiple times)
    --prepend-repo=&lt;repo path&gt;     prepend custom local repo path (can use multiple times)
    --override-repo=&lt;repo path&gt;    override repo in $REPO_FILE with custom local repo (can use multiple times)
    --repo-file=&lt;repo file&gt;        use custom repo file (default: $REPO_FILE)
    --config-file=&lt;config file&gt;    use custom config file (default: $CONFIG_FILE)
    --alias-file=&lt;alias file&gt;      use custom alias file (default: $ALIAS_FILE)
    --mask-file=&lt;mask file&gt;        use custom mask file (default: $MASK_FILE)</code></pre>

        <h2 id="install">Install, upgrade, and remove</h2>

        <pre><code>emerald install &lt;ports&gt; [pkgbuild options]
emerald upgrade &lt;ports&gt; [pkgbuild options]
emerald sysup [pkgbuild options]
emerald remove &lt;ports&gt; [pkgdel options]
emerald purge [ports]
emerald trigger [ports]</code></pre>

        <p>
            Pass <code>-y</code> when you have reviewed the transaction and want
            a non-interactive confirmation. <code>purge</code> removes selected
            ports and orphaned dependencies; inspect the proposed set before
            accepting it on a production system. <code>trigger</code> runs the
            system-maintenance hooks used after package changes.
        </p>

        <h3>Safe update sequence</h3>

        <pre><code>emerald sync
emerald upgrade emerald -y
emerald sysup</code></pre>

        <h2 id="query">Query and inspect</h2>

        <pre><code>emerald search &lt;pattern&gt;     # find available ports
emerald list                 # list all available ports
emerald info &lt;port&gt;          # show recipe metadata
emerald path &lt;port&gt;          # print repository path
emerald locate &lt;file&gt;        # locate a file in the ports tree
emerald provide &lt;file&gt;       # find the port providing a file
emerald installed            # list installed ports
emerald outdated             # list upgrades
emerald files &lt;port&gt;         # list installed files
emerald depends &lt;port&gt;       # print dependencies
emerald dependent &lt;port&gt;     # print reverse dependencies
emerald missing-deps         # report missing dependencies
emerald orphan               # list orphan ports
emerald foreign              # list ports outside repositories
emerald integrity            # check installed files
emerald is-installed &lt;port&gt;  # exit 0 if installed</code></pre>

        <p>
            The Exit status matters in scripts; <code>is-installed</code> is
            designed for that purpose.
        </p>

        <h2 id="repositories">Repositories and global options</h2>

        <p>
            The default repository file is <code>/etc/emerald.repo</code>. Each
            active line contains a local checkout, a remote URL, and optionally
            a branch. Vylen's core repository is configured as the primary
            source.
        </p>

        <pre><code>emerald sync
emerald --repo-file=/etc/emerald.repo sync
emerald --append-repo=/srv/ports/custom search my-port
emerald --prepend-repo=/srv/ports/overlay install my-port
emerald --override-repo=/srv/ports/test sysup</code></pre>

